.TH SpDrS60 1x "02. Oct 2004" "Linux" "SRCP Clients"
.SH NAME
spdrs60 \- SRCP digital model railroad controller with a look of the
German Railway SpDrS60 switch-boxes.
.\"
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spdrs60
[
.I -options
] [
.I file
]
.\"
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spdrs60
is a graphical SRCP client to comfortably control a digital model
railroad. His look has been adopted from the original German Railway
SpDrS60 switch-boxes. It is designed for use with a SRCP server as
provided by the DDL project.
.PP
.B spdrs60
can be used to access a local SRCP server, or to connect over a host
to host TCP/IP network. 
.\"
.\"
.SH OPTIONS
For now
.B spdrs60
does not implement special command-line options, but supports 
generic options of the underlying Qt-library.
.TP
.BI \-geometry \ WxH+X+Y
Sets the size and location of the main window. This may be specially
useful for displaying a full-size railroad layout.
.\"
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.BI spdrs60
Display the main window with an empty layout. Pre-loading of a
preferred layout file is controlled by the preferences dialog.
.TP
.BI spdrs60\ \-geometry\ 800x600+0+0
Display the man window in 800x600 pixel size and place it to the upper
left corner.
.\"
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP 
.I ~/.spdrs60rc
Personal spdrs60 defaults (see
.I Edit Preferences
menu).
.\"
.\"
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR centralclock (1),
.\"
.\"
.SH BUGS
There are still some bugs were is hunted for. Please send bug reports
or suggestions to Guido Scholz <guido.scholz@bayernline.de>.
.\"
.\"
.SH AUTHORS
.B spdrs60
was written by Stefan Preis <info@linux-modellbahn.de> with
